    "body": "## Problem\n\nA headful page that is being traced (`startTrace`, default `screenshots: 'checkpoints'`) can stop following its window size. After the user resizes the window, the page is still drawn at the old size in the top-left corner and the rest of the window stays blank. It stays that way until the page is reloaded.\n\nBy default, the browser must look and behave exactly like a real browser.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe trace recorder takes checkpoint screenshots with the engine's `page.screenshot({ type: 'png' })` (`src/traces/recorder.js`, `screenshot()`). For a viewport screenshot, Playwright 1.64 sends `Page.captureScreenshot` with a `clip` set to the current viewport. Chrome emulates the clip's size while it captures. If the window is resized during the capture, the emulated size can stay in place after the capture ends.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nMeasured with Chrome for Testing 156.0.8078.4 on macOS, Playwright 1.64, browser-commander 0.28 (0.32.1 has the same code):\n\n1. Start a headful Chrome and attach with `connectBrowser({ engine: 'playwright', cdpEndpoint })`.\n2. Keep taking screenshots in a loop while the window is resized in about 20 steps with `Browser.setWindowBounds`.\n3. Compare `innerWidth` with `outerWidth`.\n\n| Screenshot method | Drags where the page got stuck |\n|---|---|\n| `page.screenshot({ type: 'png' })` (Playwright) | 2 of 8 |\n| CDP `Page.captureScreenshot { format: 'png' }` (no clip) | 0 of 8 |\n| CDP `Page.captureScreenshot { fromSurface: false, captureBeyondViewport: false }` | 0 of 8 |\n| Trace checkpoints with the no-clip capture | 0 of 12 |\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nFor trace checkpoint screenshots, and any default capture of a page with no fixed viewport, use CDP `Page.captureScreenshot` without a `clip`. `captureStableViewport` already does this when `viewportSize()` is null.\n\nWorkaround in hh-job-application-automation: pass `startTrace` a `page` whose `screenshot` is the CDP capture without a clip.\n",
